⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of The Sphere of Reference
node SPW · SPW · ⟦The Sphere of Reference:SPW:a4978a⟧

WHO   — The Sphere of Reference — the lattice of allusion
WHAT  — The synth of allusion itself: the layered citations that reward the literate viewer and quietly bypass everyone else, a film built as much of references as of shots.
WHERE — SPW · Scott Pilgrim vs. the World  Framework inputs: Scott Pilgrim vs. the World (2010); O'Malley's graphic novels  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because Scott Pilgrim is a machine for recognition — its pleasure is partly the flattery of getting it — and that same density is what makes it age into a code.
HOW   — By manga speed-lines and sound-effect text, 8-bit motifs, music-scene in-jokes, and a citation rate few films have matched.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am the film made of other things — and how much of me you see is a map of exactly when and where you grew up.

